# Text files are stored with LF and checked out with LF on every platform, whatever
# core.autocrlf says (it is on by default on Windows, also on the CI runners). Generated files,
# snapshots and shell scripts are compared or run byte for byte, so a Windows checkout must not
# differ from a macOS one.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Byte-exact data: never converted, whatever it contains.
# Test mails are RFC 5322 data with CRLF line endings.
*.eml -text
# Snapshots of built mails (some keep CRLF) and of signatures and templates.
crates/mail-content/src/compose/snapshots/*.html -text
crates/mail-content/src/templates/snapshots/*.html -text
# The signed update payload, its signature and the test key of the updater tests.
app/src-tauri/src/updater/fixtures/** -text

# Binary files (git detects them anyway; stated so a new file of these types is never converted).
*.png binary
*.ico binary
*.icns binary
*.pdf binary
